# What a new Cluster Node installs before Argo CD takes over: the K3s version,
# the K3s install script and the Argo CD install manifest, each download with
# the SHA-256 it must have. Read by every bootstrap path — the local bootstrap
# script, the Hetzner cloud-init template (through Terraform) and the golden
# image build — so they cannot install different things (docs/adr/0057).
#
# Plain KEY=value lines only: no quotes, no spaces around "=", no expansion.
# Shell sources this file and Terraform parses it line by line.
#
# To change a pin, change the version, the URL and the digest together, and
# compute the digest yourself from the official source:
#
#   curl -fsSL "<url>" | sha256sum
#
# Every URL must name immutable content. The K3s installer is therefore pinned
# by commit (see https://github.com/k3s-io/k3s/commits/master/install.sh), never
# as https://get.k3s.io: that address serves whatever is on K3s's main branch
# today, and the digest stops matching the next time upstream edits the script.
#
# A change here reaches new nodes only. An existing node keeps what it has
# until it is rebuilt or its bootstrap is run again.

K3S_VERSION=v1.36.5+k3s1
K3S_INSTALLER_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/k3s-io/k3s/2977c525a2e7a487886107ce4df43630ae9b03b2/install.sh
K3S_INSTALLER_SHA256=e5cc3b3d9dfc1662c2d9be6da5abc9a4cd317d6abc3a5ffc02e3dd3248207fee

ARGOCD_VERSION=v3.5.4
ARGOCD_MANIFEST_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/v3.5.4/manifests/install.yaml
ARGOCD_MANIFEST_SHA256=1feb02cc7bacf3a379da58b0ca8c6f07d18288cd04d531dabd08816375e5e010
